# Acceptance Checklists

`docs/checklists/` states behavior that must keep working. See `docs/checklists/README.md`.

- Before changing behavior, read the checklist for the affected area, when one exists.
- Preserve every existing item unless the task intentionally changes that contract; then update the
  item in the same change.
- When a change adds behavior that must hold from now on, add an item. Leave out criteria that only
  describe the change itself.
- When a checklist disagrees with current code, a spec or an ADR, report the disagreement before
  choosing an implementation path.
- A checklist item is not evidence. Record what was actually verified in `evidence/`.

Keep item IDs stable within each functional checklist. State surface applicability and link the
accepted source. Use behavior statements, not permanent checked boxes or copies of test code.
One-time migration and feature-only criteria stay in their spec.
